## P6C — Tighten CSP with nonces

```
--- PROMPT START ---
You are working on the PRAXIS codebase. The workspace skill `praxis-conventions` is loaded — re-read the "Security boundaries" section.

# Task

`src/middleware.ts` lines ~80-89 set a CSP that allows `script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'`. The `'unsafe-inline'` is needed for:
1. Next.js inline bootstrap scripts
2. The inline JSON-LD blob in `src/app/(landing)/page.tsx`

Replace `'unsafe-inline'` with a per-request nonce.

# Step 1: Generate a nonce in middleware

In `src/middleware.ts`:

    function generateNonce(): string {
      // Edge runtime supports crypto.getRandomValues
      const arr = new Uint8Array(16);
      crypto.getRandomValues(arr);
      return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...arr));
    }

    export function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
      const nonce = generateNonce();
      // ... existing routing logic ...
      const response = /* ... existing response */;
      response.headers.set('x-nonce', nonce);
      return addSecurityHeaders(response, nonce);
    }

    function addSecurityHeaders(response: NextResponse, nonce: string): NextResponse {
      // ... existing headers ...
      response.headers.set('Content-Security-Policy',
        `default-src 'self'; ` +
        `script-src 'self' 'nonce-${nonce}' 'strict-dynamic' apis.google.com *.firebaseapp.com *.googleapis.com *.google.com *.gstatic.com www.googletagmanager.com; ` +
        `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' fonts.googleapis.com; ` +    // CSS unsafe-inline OK for Tailwind
        `img-src 'self' data: blob: *.googleapis.com *.googleusercontent.com *.gstatic.com; ` +
        `font-src 'self' fonts.gstatic.com; ` +
        // ... rest unchanged
      );
      return response;
    }

# Step 2: Use the nonce in the inline JSON-LD

In `src/app/(landing)/page.tsx`, read the nonce from headers:

    import { headers } from 'next/headers';

    export default async function LandingPage() {
      const nonce = (await headers()).get('x-nonce') ?? undefined;
      return (
        <>
          <script
            type="application/ld+json"
            nonce={nonce}
            dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: JSON.stringify(jsonLd) }}
          />
          {/* ... */}
        </>
      );
    }

# Step 3: Pass nonce to Next.js inline scripts

Next.js 16 supports nonces via the `nonce` field on script components. In `src/app/layout.tsx` (or wherever the root layout is), Next.js will auto-inject scripts. Use the documented Next.js CSP nonce pattern: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/configuring/content-security-policy

The pattern is roughly:

    import { headers } from 'next/headers';

    export default async function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
      const nonce = (await headers()).get('x-nonce');
      return (
        <html lang="en">
          <head>
            {/* nonce will be auto-applied by Next.js to its inline scripts */}
          </head>
          <body>{children}</body>
        </html>
      );
    }

Next.js reads the nonce from the `x-nonce` header set by middleware (this is a documented pattern).

